claimed: intent-eval-on-journal — the spec names a Rerun journal as the intended fixture and the first lane deliberately did not build it, so every measurement in this line has been a non-replayable live run of ten to thirty minutes. Record the model replies once into a journal, then let Eval run over the recording: a change to the decoder, the label mapping or the gate logic becomes a second-long check in the DEFAULT gate with no model at all, and Eval.regressions -- the promotion rule that has been executable-but-unexercised since lane one -- finally guards something real. A prompt change still invalidates the recording, and that is the correct signal rather than a limitation: the fingerprint says the recording no longer describes what you are asking.
